CyborgOS - HELP name shows NAME.HLP (HELP DIR, HELP CD ...)
Built in: RUN, CLS, QUIT. The commands are in C/ (CYBORGOS/C/): those on Z
(the system drive, made at boot) run as if built in - FG, PS, TOP, KILL,
RESET, WAIT, MEM, DIR, CD, CV, HELP, COPY, ERA, TYPE, RENAME, RAMDISC,
MODE, MKDIR, RMDIR, DRIVE, CLAIMS; the rest from C/ - MOUNT, PAUSE,
UNPAUSE, DUMP, REVIVE, SPEED, RMOVE, RCOPY, SLOTD, FLOPPY, NET, IPCONFIG,
NETSTAT. On the boot drive, the apps: MON, YING, YANG, RAWYING, RAWYANG;
the decision services: RAT, MODEL, NEURAL, ASK, PROBE (their test drive),
RATS, WATCH; PET (a virtual pet); RATBOX (a box of rats); RVDU (remote
displays); Pluto: ENC, DEC, KEYMGR (encode / decode files, the key manager
- HELP PLUTO)

name [args]       runs that program (from Z, the slot's drive, C/, the boot drive)
RUN [slot] name [args]   the same, even when a command has that name;
                  with a slot: runs it there (RUN 2 CRUNCH)
FG slot           that slot to the front
KILL slot         stops its program
RMOVE, RCOPY      a slot (or a program) to another machine's SLOTD (HELP RMOVE)
PAUSE, UNPAUSE slot   its program stopped where it is; going on again
RESET [slot]      that slot (or this one) as new
PS, TOP           the slots; with their speed
MEM               the memory: main RAM, the banks
DIR, DRIVE        files; the drives and devices
CV, CD            this slot's drive or device; a folder (UniDOS)
MOUNT dev letter  a device to a drive letter: MOUNT SD E (UniDOS)
MKDIR, RMDIR      folders (UniDOS)
FLOPPY from to    floppy discs: A to a folder or .DSK, and back (HELP FLOPPY)
NET [M4]          the network: on (an M4 board), off, a page fetched
CLAIMS            hardware the programs have claimed; CLAIMS TAKE one back
WAIT, CLS, QUIT   until no program runs; clear; end CyborgOS
MODE [m]          this slot's screen
COPY, ERA, TYPE, RENAME   files (HELP COPY ...)
RAMDISC           RAM discs
IDE: (any word ending ":")      CV to that drive or device

Control + 1-9, 0: that slot to the front (more than 10 slots: the number
twice for 11-20)   Control + ESC: TOP
